 "notes": [
  "THE ROYAL CHARTER (client/scenes/court/pass_view.gd), from pass.png (art/slices/pass.json), every band where it was painted: the header 0..400, the progress strip 400..540, the FREE / ROYAL headings 540..592, the tiers from 592 in a list that grows to the foot, and the foot (the pedestal and CLAIM ALL) pinned to the screen's foot from 1226.",
  "timer: the season's time left in the EMPTY plate beside the hourglass (inside x 694..846, y 288..328); season: its name and day in the plate under it (inside x 694..914, y 343..379). Garamond as the Court's lines, ivory.",
  "tier: the tier reached, in the big medallion's dark centre (x 206..287, y 433..515; centre 246.5, 474), Cinzel 40 in the painting's gold. bar_fill: the painted gold along the channel's inside (x 322..683, y 447..466) to the tier's points; points: those points against the tier's, in the plate under the bar (inside x 413..588, y 480..521).",
  "info_coin / info: the Tax Cart's painted (i) coin (chests/info), drawn down to 50 beside the points plate, under a 104 x 72 tap area: HOW THE CHARTER FILLS. progress: the medallion and the bar are a tap for it too.",
  "unlock_word / unlock_price: the UNLOCK plate's word, lifted and set in type where it was painted (caps x 760..870, y 441..461: Cinzel 29, ivory) -- UNLOCK while the royal lane is shut, ROYAL once it is open -- and the EMPTY price plate under it (inside x 730..889, y 482..516): the diamonds and the App Store's price, or the lane's state. unlock: the whole plate is the tap.",
  "tier_row: row 3 repeated at the painting's pitch (127): the plate, the medallion and the chain; the free tile at x 253 and the royal at x 647 (their own crops), each with its reward's picture in the tile's middle (pic_*), what it pays in its lower right corner (amount_*, and gem_* when a crowned tier also pays diamonds), the tier in the medallion's dark centre (medal: centre 385.5, 64 in the row; Cinzel 30), the ROYAL heading's crown on the medallion of a crowned tier, CLAIM where the painting set it on row 2 (13 in, 71 down the tile, hanging 10 under it), the tick seal on a claimed tile's top right corner as row 1 has it (drawn down to the painting's 56), and the padlock in a shut royal tile's lower right as rows 3-5 have it (drawn down to the painting's 30).",
  "pedestal: the Charter's frame (frames/charter_square, 175 x 202 at its own scale) round the lord's face, standing on the pedestal's slab (its foot at y 1448) where the painting stood its trophy; pedestal_seal its tick once tier 50's royal reward is claimed. claim_all: CLAIM ALL drawn over its own painted place, dimmed when nothing waits.",
  "A tile's CLAIM is the painting's own plate, drawn on the tile, not a button: the tile itself is the tap (hit_free / hit_royal, 190x116), so the plate is never a second, smaller target for the same claim."
 ],
